IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part II (ss 56 to 65.2): employment support measures and the National
-- Employment Service. Piece ei2. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30. Seat: the person who is, or asks to be, helped by an employment support measure, or is referred by the
-- National Employment Service.
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld). ss 59, 61 to 63: the Commission's powers to establish measures, give financial assistance and make
-- agreements; the worker or participant is liable to them (and, once assistance is given, has a claim to the terms on which it
-- is given). s 60(2)(b): the worker's claim not to be discriminated against in a referral; the service's duty. s 64: the
-- person's disability (no review under s 112) and the Commission's immunity. s 65: the person's duty to repay; the Crown's
-- claim. s 65.1: the Commission's power to impose a penalty; the person's liability; s 65.1(3): the person's immunity; (4):
-- the Commission's power to rescind. s 65.2: the Crown's claim as a debt and power to deduct; the person's immunity after 72 months.
--
-- Section 56 (the purpose) carries no condition and computes nothing: it is carried as a named STRING, as the phrasebook says
-- (9.3). Section 60(3) (regulations) is inert machinery; ss 57(3), 60(4), 60(5), 63(2) and 63.1 are repealed (coverage table).
-- Where a defined term is encoded by another piece, the module takes its outcome as a plain input:
--   the employee's premium refund of s 96(4): section 96(4), piece ei3;  the Emergency Response Benefit: Part VIII.4, piece ei6;
--   review under s 112: section 112, piece ei4;  the Federal Court certificate and debts: piece ei4.
-- Regulation 76.11 (piece er4) adapts the definition of "insured participant" in s 58 for a person under a provincial plan:
-- it is a separate input of the s 58 rule (fork ei2-F12).

§ `Section 56 - purpose`

-- src:1050 | Purpose
-- src:1051 | 56 The purpose of this Part is to help maintain a sustainable employment insurance system through the establishment of employment support measures and the maintenance of a national employment service.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 56 (src:1050-1051)
`s 56 the purpose of Part II` MEANS
    "56 The purpose of this Part is to help maintain a sustainable employment insurance system through the establishment of employment support measures and the maintenance of a national employment service."

§ `Section 57 - guidelines, and working in concert`

-- (1)(d.1): "availability of assistance under the measures in either official language where there is significant demand for
-- that assistance in that language": the condition bites only where there is significant demand.
-- src:1058 | (d.1) availability of assistance under the measures in either official language where there is significant demand for that assistance in that language;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 57(1)(d.1) (src:1058)
GIVEN `there is significant demand for assistance in an official language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `assistance under the measures is available in that official language` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(1)(d.1) assistance is available in either official language where there is significant demand` IF
    (NOT `there is significant demand for assistance in an official language`) OR `assistance under the measures is available in that official language`

-- (1)(e): "commitment by persons receiving assistance under the measures to (i) achieving the goals of the assistance, (ii) taking
-- primary responsibility for identifying their employment needs and locating services necessary to allow them to meet those needs,
-- and (iii) if appropriate, sharing the cost of the assistance". The participant's side of the guidelines: what the person
-- receiving assistance is expected to commit to. (iii) bites only if sharing is appropriate.
-- src:1059 | (e) commitment by persons receiving assistance under the measures to
-- src:1060 | (i) achieving the goals of the assistance,
-- src:1061 | (ii) taking primary responsibility for identifying their employment needs and locating services necessary to allow them to meet those needs, and
-- src:1062 | (iii) if appropriate, sharing the cost of the assistance; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 57(1)(e) (src:1059-1062)
GIVEN `commitment by persons receiving assistance to achieving the goals of the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `commitment by persons receiving assistance to taking primary responsibility for identifying their employment needs and locating services necessary to allow them to meet those needs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sharing the cost of the assistance is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `commitment by persons receiving assistance to sharing the cost of the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(1)(e) the commitment expected of persons receiving assistance is made` IF
        `commitment by persons receiving assistance to achieving the goals of the assistance`
    AND `commitment by persons receiving assistance to taking primary responsibility for identifying their employment needs and locating services necessary to allow them to meet those needs`
    AND ((NOT `sharing the cost of the assistance is appropriate`) OR `commitment by persons receiving assistance to sharing the cost of the assistance`)

-- (1): "Employment support measures under this Part shall be established in accordance with the following guidelines: (a) ...
-- (f)". A measure is established in accordance with them when each holds; (d.1) and (e) are the rules above.
-- src:1052 | Guidelines
-- src:1053 | 57 (1) Employment support measures under this Part shall be established in accordance with the following guidelines:
-- src:1054 | (a) harmonization with provincial employment initiatives to ensure that there is no unnecessary overlap or duplication;
-- src:1055 | (b) reduction of dependency on unemployment benefits by helping individuals obtain or keep employment;
-- src:1056 | (c) co-operation and partnership with other governments, employers, community-based organizations and other interested organizations;
-- src:1057 | (d) flexibility to allow significant decisions about implementation to be made at a local level;
-- src:1058 | (d.1) availability of assistance under the measures in either official language where there is significant demand for that assistance in that language;
-- src:1059 | (e) commitment by persons receiving assistance under the measures to
-- src:1060 | (i) achieving the goals of the assistance,
-- src:1061 | (ii) taking primary responsibility for identifying their employment needs and locating services necessary to allow them to meet those needs, and
-- src:1062 | (iii) if appropriate, sharing the cost of the assistance; and
-- src:1063 | (f) implementation of the measures within a framework for evaluating their success in assisting persons to obtain or keep employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 57(1) (src:1052-1063)
GIVEN `harmonization with provincial employment initiatives to ensure that there is no unnecessary overlap or duplication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reduction of dependency on unemployment benefits by helping individuals obtain or keep employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `co-operation and partnership with other governments, employers, community-based organizations and other interested organizations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `flexibility to allow significant decisions about implementation to be made at a local level` IS A BOOLEAN
      `assistance is available in either official language where there is significant demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commitment expected of persons receiving assistance is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `implementation of the measures within a framework for evaluating their success in assisting persons to obtain or keep employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(1) the measures are established in accordance with the guidelines` IF
        `harmonization with provincial employment initiatives to ensure that there is no unnecessary overlap or duplication`
    AND `reduction of dependency on unemployment benefits by helping individuals obtain or keep employment`
    AND `co-operation and partnership with other governments, employers, community-based organizations and other interested organizations`
    AND `flexibility to allow significant decisions about implementation to be made at a local level`
    AND `assistance is available in either official language where there is significant demand`
    AND `the commitment expected of persons receiving assistance is made`
    AND `implementation of the measures within a framework for evaluating their success in assisting persons to obtain or keep employment`

-- (2): "To give effect to the purpose and guidelines of this Part, the Commission shall work in concert with provincial
-- governments and consult with workers and employers to align employment support measures with labour market needs."
-- src:1064 | Working in concert and consultations
-- src:1065 | (2) To give effect to the purpose and guidelines of this Part, the Commission shall work in concert with provincial governments and consult with workers and employers to align employment support measures with labour market needs.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 57(2) (src:1064-1065)
GIVEN `the Commission works in concert with provincial governments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission consults with workers and employers to align employment support measures with labour market needs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 57(2) the Commission has worked in concert and consulted as the Act requires` IF
        `the Commission works in concert with provincial governments`
    AND `the Commission consults with workers and employers to align employment support measures with labour market needs`

§ `Section 58 - insured participant`

-- "In this Part, insured participant means (a) an insured person who requests assistance under an employment support measure
-- and, when requesting the assistance, is a person for whom a benefit period is established or whose benefit period has ended
-- within the previous 60 months or a person who paid, in at least 3 of the last 10 years, employee's premiums that did not
-- entitle them to a refund under subsection 96(4); and (b) an insured person who requests assistance under an employment
-- support measure and, when requesting assistance, is a person who was in receipt of the employment insurance emergency
-- response benefit within the previous 60 months." The 60th month counts (the keel's fork F4, and ei2-F10 here). Regulation 76.11
-- (out of range: Regulations s 76.11, piece er4) adds a third class (fork ei2-F12).
-- src:1067 | Definition of insured participant
-- src:1068 | 58 In this Part, insured participant means
-- src:1069 | (a) an insured person who requests assistance under an employment support measure and, when requesting the assistance, is a person for whom a benefit period is established or whose benefit period has ended within the previous 60 months or a person who paid, in at least 3 of the last 10 years, employee’s premiums that did not entitle them to a refund under subsection 96(4); and
-- src:1070 | (b) an insured person who requests assistance under an employment support measure and, when requesting assistance, is a person who was in receipt of the employment insurance emergency response benefit within the previous 60 months.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 58 (src:1067-1070)
GIVEN `the person is employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person requests assistance under an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit period is established for the person when requesting the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person's benefit period ended, if it has ended` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the number of the last 10 years in which the person paid employee's premiums that did not entitle them to a refund under subsection 96(4)` IS A NUMBER
      `the last day on which the person was in receipt of the employment insurance emergency response benefit, if ever` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the person requests the assistance` IS A DATE
      `the person is within the definition as adapted by regulation 76.11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 58 the person is an insured participant` IF
        `s 2(1) insured person` `the person is employed in insurable employment` `the person has been employed in insurable employment`
    AND `the person requests assistance under an employment support measure`
    AND (   `a benefit period is established for the person when requesting the assistance`
         OR `within the previous 60 months` `the day on which the person's benefit period ended, if it has ended` `the day on which the person requests the assistance`
         OR `the number of the last 10 years in which the person paid employee's premiums that did not entitle them to a refund under subsection 96(4)` AT LEAST 3
         OR `within the previous 60 months` `the last day on which the person was in receipt of the employment insurance emergency response benefit, if ever` `the day on which the person requests the assistance`
         OR `the person is within the definition as adapted by regulation 76.11`)
    WHERE
        `within the previous 60 months` eventDay requestDay MEANS
            CONSIDER eventDay
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST e  THEN e AT MOST requestDay AND requestDay AT MOST (`add months` e 60)

§ `Section 59 - employment support measures`

-- "The Commission may establish employment support measures to help insured participants and other workers, including workers
-- in groups underrepresented in the labour market, to obtain or keep employment, including measures to (a) ... (d)". The
-- four kinds are examples ("including"): the kinds are the nouns of ei2-nouns. The power is exercised where the measure is
-- meant to help insured participants and other workers to obtain or keep employment.
-- src:1071 | Employment support measures
-- src:1072 | 59 The Commission may establish employment support measures to help insured participants and other workers, including workers in groups underrepresented in the labour market, to obtain or keep employment, including measures to
-- src:1073 | (a) provide insured participants with courses or programs of instruction or training;
-- src:1074 | (b) provide insured participants with employment opportunities or provide employment support;
-- src:1075 | (c) provide workers with employment assistance services; and
-- src:1076 | (d) support research, innovation or partnerships related to helping workers to prepare for, obtain or keep employment and to be productive participants in the labour market.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 59 (src:1071-1076)
GIVEN `the measure is to help insured participants and other workers, including workers in groups underrepresented in the labour market, to obtain or keep employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 59 the Commission may establish the employment support measure` IF
    `the measure is to help insured participants and other workers, including workers in groups underrepresented in the labour market, to obtain or keep employment`

§ `Section 60 - the National Employment Service`

-- (1): "The Commission shall maintain a national employment service to provide information on employment opportunities across
-- Canada to help workers find suitable employment and help employers find suitable workers."
-- src:1077 | National employment service
-- src:1078 | 60 (1) The Commission shall maintain a national employment service to provide information on employment opportunities across Canada to help workers find suitable employment and help employers find suitable workers.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 60(1) (src:1077-1078)
GIVEN `the Commission maintains a national employment service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service provides information on employment opportunities across Canada to help workers find suitable employment and help employers find suitable workers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 60(1) the Commission has maintained the national employment service as the Act requires` IF
        `the Commission maintains a national employment service`
    AND `the service provides information on employment opportunities across Canada to help workers find suitable employment and help employers find suitable workers`

-- (2)(a): "collect information concerning employment for workers and workers seeking employment and, to the extent the
-- Commission considers necessary, make the information available with a view to assisting workers to obtain employment for
-- which they are suited and assisting employers to obtain workers most suitable to their needs".
-- src:1079 | Duties of the Commission
-- src:1080 | (2) The Commission shall
-- src:1081 | (a) collect information concerning employment for workers and workers seeking employment and, to the extent the Commission considers necessary, make the information available with a view to assisting workers to obtain employment for which they are suited and assisting employers to obtain workers most suitable to their needs; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 60(2)(a) (src:1079-1081)
GIVEN `the Commission collects information concerning employment for workers and workers seeking employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission makes the information available to the extent it considers necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 60(2)(a) the Commission has collected and made available the information as the Act requires` IF
        `the Commission collects information concerning employment for workers and workers seeking employment`
    AND `the Commission makes the information available to the extent it considers necessary`

-- (2)(b): "ensure that in referring a worker seeking employment there will be no discrimination on a prohibited ground of
-- discrimination within the meaning of the Canadian Human Rights Act or because of political affiliation, but nothing in this
-- paragraph prohibits the national employment service from giving effect to (i) any limitation, specification or preference
-- based on a bona fide occupational requirement, or (ii) any special program, plan or arrangement mentioned in section 16 of
-- the Canadian Human Rights Act." A referral is within the paragraph when it does not discriminate on those grounds, or
-- the difference is a limitation based on a bona fide occupational requirement or a special programme.
-- src:1082 | (b) ensure that in referring a worker seeking employment there will be no discrimination on a prohibited ground of discrimination within the meaning of the Canadian Human Rights Act or because of political affiliation, but nothing in this paragraph prohibits the national employment service from giving effect to
-- src:1083 | (i) any limitation, specification or preference based on a bona fide occupational requirement, or
-- src:1084 | (ii) any special program, plan or arrangement mentioned in section 16 of the Canadian Human Rights Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 60(2)(b) (src:1082-1084)
GIVEN `the referral discriminates on a prohibited ground of discrimination within the meaning of the Canadian Human Rights Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the referral discriminates because of political affiliation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the referral gives effect to a limitation, specification or preference based on a bona fide occupational requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the referral gives effect to a special program, plan or arrangement mentioned in section 16 of the Canadian Human Rights Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 60(2)(b) the referral is as the Act requires` IF
       (NOT (`the referral discriminates on a prohibited ground of discrimination within the meaning of the Canadian Human Rights Act` OR `the referral discriminates because of political affiliation`))
    OR `the referral gives effect to a limitation, specification or preference based on a bona fide occupational requirement`
    OR `the referral gives effect to a special program, plan or arrangement mentioned in section 16 of the Canadian Human Rights Act`

§ `Sections 61 to 64 - assistance, agreements and no review`

-- 61: "The Commission may, in accordance with terms and conditions approved by the Treasury Board, provide financial assistance
-- for the purpose of implementing employment support measures."
-- src:1089 | Financial assistance
-- src:1090 | 61 The Commission may, in accordance with terms and conditions approved by the Treasury Board, provide financial assistance for the purpose of implementing employment support measures.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 61 (src:1089-1090)
GIVEN `the terms and conditions are approved by the Treasury Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is for the purpose of implementing employment support measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61 the Commission may provide the financial assistance` IF
        `the terms and conditions are approved by the Treasury Board`
    AND `the assistance is for the purpose of implementing employment support measures`

-- 62: "The Commission may, with the approval of the Minister, enter into an agreement or arrangement for the administration of
-- employment support measures on its behalf by a department, board or agency of the Government of Canada, another government
-- or government agency in Canada or any other public or private organization."
-- src:1091 | Agreements for administering employment support measures
-- src:1092 | 62 The Commission may, with the approval of the Minister, enter into an agreement or arrangement for the administration of employment support measures on its behalf by a department, board or agency of the Government of Canada, another government or government agency in Canada or any other public or private organization.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 62 (src:1091-1092)
GIVEN `the Minister has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is for the administration of employment support measures on the Commission's behalf by a department, board or agency of the Government of Canada, another government or government agency in Canada or any other public or private organization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 62 the Commission may enter into the agreement or arrangement` IF
        `the Minister has approved`
    AND `the agreement is for the administration of employment support measures on the Commission's behalf by a department, board or agency of the Government of Canada, another government or government agency in Canada or any other public or private organization`

-- 63(1): "The Commission may, with the approval of the Minister, enter into an agreement with a government or government agency in
-- Canada or any other public or private organization to provide for the payment of contributions for all or a portion of (a) any
-- costs of measures implemented by the government, government agency or organization that are consistent with the purpose and
-- guidelines of this Part; and (b) any administration costs that the government, government agency or organization incurs in
-- implementing the measures."
-- src:1093 | Agreements for paying costs of similar benefits and measures
-- src:1094 | 63 (1) The Commission may, with the approval of the Minister, enter into an agreement with a government or government agency in Canada or any other public or private organization to provide for the payment of contributions for all or a portion of
-- src:1095 | (a) any costs of measures implemented by the government, government agency or organization that are consistent with the purpose and guidelines of this Part; and
-- src:1096 | (b) any administration costs that the government, government agency or organization incurs in implementing the measures.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 63(1) (src:1093-1096)
GIVEN `the Minister has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is with a government or government agency in Canada or any other public or private organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributions are for all or a portion of the costs of measures that are consistent with the purpose and guidelines of Part II` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributions are for all or a portion of the administration costs incurred in implementing the measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 63(1) the Commission may enter into the agreement to pay contributions` IF
        `the Minister has approved`
    AND `the agreement is with a government or government agency in Canada or any other public or private organization`
    AND (   `the contributions are for all or a portion of the costs of measures that are consistent with the purpose and guidelines of Part II`
         OR `the contributions are for all or a portion of the administration costs incurred in implementing the measures`)

-- 64: "A decision of the Commission made in relation to employment support measures, other than a decision under section 65.1, is
-- not subject to review under section 112." (Section 112 is piece ei4's.) A decision under s 65.1 is outside the rule: the
-- section says nothing about it, so NOTHING.
-- src:1099 | No appeal
-- src:1100 | 64 A decision of the Commission made in relation to employment support measures, other than a decision under section 65.1, is not subject to review under section 112.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 64 (src:1099-1100)
GIVEN `the decision of the Commission is made in relation to employment support measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is a decision under section 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 64 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` IS
    IF     `the decision of the Commission is made in relation to employment support measures`
       AND (NOT `the decision is a decision under section 65.1`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 65 - liability for repayments`

-- "A person is liable to repay the following amounts paid under section 61: (a) principal and interest on a loan to the person;
-- (b) an amount paid on a guarantee or suretyship of a loan made to the person; and (c) an amount paid to the person to which the
-- person is not entitled." The total repayable is the sum of the three; each amount is 0 where there is none.
-- src:1101 | Liability for repayments
-- src:1102 | 65 A person is liable to repay the following amounts paid under section 61:
-- src:1103 | (a) principal and interest on a loan to the person;
-- src:1104 | (b) an amount paid on a guarantee or suretyship of a loan made to the person; and
-- src:1105 | (c) an amount paid to the person to which the person is not entitled.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 65 (src:1101-1105)
GIVEN `the principal and interest on a loan to the person` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid on a guarantee or suretyship of a loan made to the person` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid to the person to which the person is not entitled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 65 the amount the person is liable to repay` IS
    `the principal and interest on a loan to the person` PLUS `the amount paid on a guarantee or suretyship of a loan made to the person` PLUS `the amount paid to the person to which the person is not entitled`

§ `Section 65.1 - penalties`

-- (1): "The Commission may impose on a person to whom financial assistance has been provided under section 61 a penalty for each
-- of the following acts or omissions if the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that the person has
-- (a) in relation to an application or request for the assistance, (i) made a representation that the person knew was false or
-- misleading, or (ii) made a declaration that the person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts; or
-- (b) without good cause failed to attend, carry out or complete the course, program or activity for which the assistance was
-- provided or was expelled from it."
-- src:1106 | Penalties
-- src:1107 | 65.1 (1) The Commission may impose on a person to whom financial assistance has been provided under section 61 a penalty for each of the following acts or omissions if the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that the person has
-- src:1108 | (a) in relation to an application or request for the assistance,
-- src:1109 | (i) made a representation that the person knew was false or misleading, or
-- src:1110 | (ii) made a declaration that the person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts; or
-- src:1111 | (b) without good cause failed to attend, carry out or complete the course, program or activity for which the assistance was provided or was expelled from it.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 65.1(1) (src:1106-1111)
GIVEN `financial assistance has been provided to the person under section 61` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish an act or omission mentioned in subsection 65.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in relation to an application or request for the assistance, made a representation that the person knew was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in relation to an application or request for the assistance, made a declaration that the person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `without good cause failed to attend, carry out or complete the course, program or activity for which the assistance was provided, or was expelled from it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65.1(1) the Commission may impose a penalty on the person` IF
        `financial assistance has been provided to the person under section 61`
    AND `the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish an act or omission mentioned in subsection 65.1(1)`
    AND (   `in relation to an application or request for the assistance, made a representation that the person knew was false or misleading`
         OR `in relation to an application or request for the assistance, made a declaration that the person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts`
         OR `without good cause failed to attend, carry out or complete the course, program or activity for which the assistance was provided, or was expelled from it`)

-- (2): "The Commission may set the amount of the penalty for each act or omission at not more than the amount of the financial
-- assistance that was provided."
-- src:1112 | Maximum penalty
-- src:1113 | (2) The Commission may set the amount of the penalty for each act or omission at not more than the amount of the financial assistance that was provided.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 65.1(2) (src:1112-1113)
GIVEN `the amount of the financial assistance that was provided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 65.1(2) the most the Commission may set as the amount of the penalty` IS
    `the amount of the financial assistance that was provided`

-- (3): "The penalty shall not be imposed if (a) a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person; or
-- (b) 36 months have passed since the day on which the act or omission occurred." Thirty-six months have passed once the day is
-- after the 36-month anniversary (fork ei2-F10).
-- src:1114 | Limitation on imposition of penalties
-- src:1115 | (3) The penalty shall not be imposed if
-- src:1116 | (a) a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person; or
-- src:1117 | (b) 36 months have passed since the day on which the act or omission occurred.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 65.1(3) (src:1114-1117)
GIVEN `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the act or omission occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the penalty would be imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65.1(3) the penalty shall not be imposed` IF
       `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person`
    OR `the day on which the penalty would be imposed` ABOVE (`add months` `the day on which the act or omission occurred` 36)

-- (4): "The Commission may rescind the imposition of the penalty, or reduce the penalty, on the presentation of new facts or on
-- being satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact."
-- src:1118 | Rescission, etc., of penalty
-- src:1119 | (4) The Commission may rescind the imposition of the penalty, or reduce the penalty, on the presentation of new facts or on being satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 65.1(4) (src:1118-1119)
GIVEN `new facts have been presented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65.1(4) the Commission may rescind the imposition of the penalty, or reduce it` IF
       `new facts have been presented`
    OR `the Commission is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact`

§ `Section 65.2 - debts due to the Crown`

-- (1): "Amounts repayable under section 65 and penalties under section 65.1 are debts due to Her Majesty and are recoverable in
-- the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act."
-- src:1120 | Debts due to the Crown
-- src:1121 | 65.2 (1) Amounts repayable under section 65 and penalties under section 65.1 are debts due to Her Majesty and are recoverable in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 65.2(1) (src:1120-1121)
GIVEN `the amount is repayable under section 65 or is a penalty under section 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65.2(1) the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` IS
    IF `the amount is repayable under section 65 or is a penalty under section 65.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): "If an amount becomes payable to the person under section 61, the amount of their indebtedness to Her Majesty may be
-- recovered out of the amount payable."
-- src:1122 | Recovery by deduction
-- src:1123 | (2) If an amount becomes payable to the person under section 61, the amount of their indebtedness to Her Majesty may be recovered out of the amount payable.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 65.2(2) (src:1122-1123)
GIVEN `the person owes an amount of indebtedness to Her Majesty under subsection 65.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an amount becomes payable to the person under section 61` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65.2(2) the indebtedness may be recovered out of the amount payable` IF
        `the person owes an amount of indebtedness to Her Majesty under subsection 65.2(1)`
    AND `an amount becomes payable to the person under section 61`

-- (3): "No amount due under this section may be recovered more than 72 months after the day on which the liability arose." Unlike
-- s 47, this section has no rule that the limit stops running while an appeal is pending (see NOTES.md, finding 8).
-- src:1124 | Limitation
-- src:1125 | (3) No amount due under this section may be recovered more than 72 months after the day on which the liability arose.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 65.2(3) (src:1124-1125)
GIVEN `the day on which the liability arose` IS A DATE
      `the day on which recovery would be attempted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 65.2(3) the amount may still be recovered` IF
    `the day on which recovery would be attempted` AT MOST (`add months` `the day on which the liability arose` 72)
